{"n": 1028, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1028.webp", "text": "51-763\n\n5171452 INSTALLING BOTH SIDE MEMBER COVER PANELS (M-SYSTEM)\n\nPainting:\n\nThe side member panels are supplied with a primo coat and substructure paint coats, so that only\nthe final paint coat has to be sprayed on.\n\nProcedures: BMW Plastic Part Painting.\n\nBMW acrylic paint + 20 % BMW softface additive.\n\nCautiont\n\nMaximum enamel baking temperature; 50° C (122° F) — higher temperatures could lead to\ndeformation,\n\nTaping:\n— Soak a clean cloth in washing gasoline or cold cleaner and wipe off the surface for adhesive\ntape.\n\n— Position and press double-sided adhesive tape on side members (heat hand warm prior to\napplication!).\n\n— Pull off protective backing and mount the part, pressing on at least 5 to 10 seconds: The\ninitial adhesion can be improved by warming the body.\n\nPaint side member panels (see ‘’Painting’).\nPaste template on side members as shown and\nmark location of holes.\n\nPunch centers and drill 9 mm (0.354\") dia.\n\nholes with a spiral drill,\na Deburr and coat edges of holes with zinc dust\n\n= _— paint,\nees Treat side member cavities with a body cavity\na | sealing compound to isolate any burrs from\nL= \" drilling which might have fallen in the side\nee |) members.\n\n30 51510\n\n30 $1 512\n\nW 51513\n\nRemove screws on bottom of side panel.\nLoosen wheel house shells.\n\nMount side member panel temporarily.\n\nMark location of holes on rear wheel house\nopening, punch centers and drill 5 mm\n(0.197\"') dia. holes.\n\nTake off side member panel again.\nDeburr and cost edges of holes with zinc dust\npaint.\n\nInstall grommets (1) in side member.\n\nInsert clips (2) in side member panel.\n\nInstall sealing tape (3).\n\nNote:\n\nCoat of PVC must be removed in area of holes\nfor installation of grommets.", "words": [["51-763", 0.4772, 0.0285, 0.5471, 0.0524], ["5171452", 0.0228, 0.071, 0.074, 0.0829], ["INSTALLING", 0.0871, 0.0716, 0.152, 0.0836], ["BOTH", 0.155